q
1 0 0 1 0 0 cm  BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
q
1 0 0 1 51 770.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 5 Tm /F2 18 Tf 23 TL 201.1248 0 Td (CO5 \226 AT2) Tj T* -201.1248 0 Td ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 747.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm /F1 11 Tf 15 TL 132.6338 0 Td (Cybersecurity Assessment \226 Detailed Answers) Tj T* -132.6338 0 Td ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 557.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 158 Tm /F2 12 Tf 17 TL (1. A mid-sized financial organization operates several legacy Windows servers where) Tj T* (multiple RPC services remain exposed due to delayed patching cycles caused by) Tj T* (operational constraints. Recently, abnormal traffic patterns and unauthorized) Tj T* (connection attempts have been observed within the internal network. As a security) Tj T* (analyst, evaluate how attackers could exploit these RPC vulnerabilities to gain) Tj T* (unauthorized access and escalate privileges. Assess the level of risk associated with) Tj T* (delaying patches in such environments and justify whether immediate patch) Tj T* (deployment or controlled maintenance scheduling is more appropriate. Recommend) Tj T* (suitable mitigation strategies to reduce exposure without affecting business) Tj T* (continuity.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 532.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 5.5 Tm /F2 10.5 Tf 16 TL (Understanding the Security Problem) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 430.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 85.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 16 TL .330045 Tw (Remote Procedure Call \(RPC\) services allow programs on different systems to communicate and request) Tj T* 0 Tw .012471 Tw (services across a network. On legacy Windows servers, exposed and unpatched RPC services can create) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.080299 Tw (a significant attack surface. The abnormal internal traffic and unauthorized connection attempts indicate) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.839545 Tw (that an attacker, malware infection, or compromised internal account may already be attempting to) Tj T* 0 Tw 5.139899 Tw (discover vulnerable systems. Because the organization handles financial information, successful) Tj T* 0 Tw (compromise could affect confidentiality, integrity, availability, and regulatory compliance.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 407.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 5.5 Tm /F2 10.5 Tf 16 TL (How Attackers Could Exploit the Exposure) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 305.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 85.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 16 TL .38719 Tw (Attackers may first identify systems exposing vulnerable RPC interfaces through internal reconnaissance.) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.221738 Tw (Known software flaws, weak authentication, or insecure service configurations could then be abused to) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.132971 Tw (obtain unauthorized access. Depending on the vulnerability and the privileges of the affected service, a) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.206326 Tw (successful compromise may allow an attacker to execute unauthorized actions, access sensitive) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.066761 Tw (information, or move laterally to other servers. If a vulnerable service operates with elevated privileges, the) Tj T* 0 Tw (impact may include privilege escalation and wider compromise of the Windows environment.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 282.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 5.5 Tm /F2 10.5 Tf 16 TL (Risk of Delaying Patches) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 180.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 85.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 16 TL 1.411639 Tw (The risk level is high because legacy systems often lack modern security protections and may contain) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.032608 Tw (publicly known vulnerabilities. Delayed patching increases the time during which attackers can identify and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.021963 Tw (target weaknesses. Internal exposure is particularly dangerous because attackers who compromise one) Tj T* 0 Tw .298349 Tw (endpoint can use it as a starting point for lateral movement. In a financial organization, the consequences) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.080262 Tw (may include unauthorized access to financial records, service disruption, data theft, fraud, and reputational) Tj T* 0 Tw (damage.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 157.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 5.5 Tm /F2 10.5 Tf 16 TL (Immediate Patching vs Controlled Maintenance) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 51 55.88976 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 85.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 16 TL 3.468738 Tw (Immediate emergency patching is justified when there is evidence of active exploitation, a critical) Tj T* 0 Tw .512721 Tw (vulnerability with a reliable attack path, or direct exposure of highly sensitive systems. However, applying) Tj T* 0 Tw .236353 Tw (patches without testing may create operational failures on legacy servers. Therefore, where an immediate) Tj T* 0 Tw .384471 Tw (shutdown or patch is not feasible, a controlled emergency maintenance schedule should be used. Critical) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.043238 Tw (systems should be prioritized, patches should be tested on representative systems where possible, and) Tj T* 0 Tw (compensating controls should remain active until patching is complete.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
 

Q

